{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Barcode",
    "description": "GET /barcode/resolve is every scan's front door: unknown code 404, retired card 410 Gone, otherwise the code's type and a live payload for it.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Barcode Detail",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/barcode/detail",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "barcode",
            "detail"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "code",
              "value": "",
              "description": "The clicked/scanned barcode string.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Full detail for one barcode (click-through from the history list). Same\nrich payload as /resolve, tenancy-scoped for CLIENT logins."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Employee Barcode Action",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/employees/{{employee_id}}/barcode",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "employees",
            "{{employee_id}}",
            "barcode"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "employee_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Reissue a card (damaged/lost) or deactivate it (worker left). Deactivation\nNEVER deletes the employee or their history \u2014 it retires the scannable code.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"action\": \"\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Barcode Orders",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/barcode/orders",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "barcode",
            "orders"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "Rows to return (1-200).",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Orders that have generated barcodes \u2014 the picker. Unique per order_number.\nShows minted count + generated date range so the user picks the right order.\n\nPAGED, newest minting first: this grows by one row per order for the life of\nthe factory."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "List Order Sku Options",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/barcode/orders/{{order_id}}/skus",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "barcode",
            "orders",
            "{{order_id}}",
            "skus"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "order_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "SKU + style options to populate the filter dropdowns for this order."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Material Barcodes",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/barcode/materials",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "barcode",
            "materials"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "category",
              "value": "",
              "description": "LEATHER | LINING | ACCESSORY",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "active_only",
              "value": "True",
              "description": "Hide retired labels.",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "kind",
              "value": "",
              "description": "LOT = shelf labels only \u00b7 SHEET = hide labels only \u00b7 omit for both, each lot followed by its own hides.",
              "disabled": true
            },
            {
              "key": "limit",
              "value": "50",
              "description": "Rows to return (1-200).",
              "disabled": false
            },
            {
              "key": "offset",
              "value": "0",
              "description": "Rows to skip before returning `limit` rows.",
              "disabled": false
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "THE MATERIAL-BARCODE SCREEN \u2014 lot labels AND hide labels.\n\nThe barcode section had screens for pieces and employee cards but\nnone for material lots \u2014 so a lot minted a code at creation and nobody could\nreprint it once the first label was lost or damaged.\n\nHIDE LABELS ARE HERE TOO. Creating a leather lot with `sheets` mints a\nLEATHER_SHEET barcode per skin (POST /materials/lots returns them in\n`sheets`), and this screen used to list only the three LOT types \u2014 so those\ncodes existed in the registry and no screen could ever reprint them. Branch\non `kind`:\n\n    LOT     one sticker for the shelf: article \u00b7 colour \u00b7 thickness \u00b7 total\n    SHEET   one sticker per skin:      article \u00b7 colour \u00b7 that hide's dcm\n\nA SHEET row carries `sheet_id`, `dcm`, `sheet_status` (IN_STOCK / ALLOCATED\n/ ISSUED / CONSUMED \u2026) and `cutting_row_id`; all four are null on a LOT row.\nEach row carries `code` (encode as Code128) and `label_line` (typeset\nunderneath as text), the same convention as POST /barcode/print. A row with\n`status: retired` belongs to a retired lot or hide: show it greyed, do not\nprint it."
      },
      "response": []
    },
